- In June, 1/4 of the employees' contracts expired.
- Number of employees whose contracts expired = \( \frac{1}{4} \times 40 = 10 \, \text{employees} \).
- Remaining employees in June = \( 40 - 10 = 30 \, \text{employees} \).

