Half of the alphabet is \( 26 \div 2 = 13 \) letters.
So, Elise writes 13 letters here.
3. **Re-writing and reviewing everything she has already written**:
At this point, Elise has written \( 52 + 13 = 65 \) letters.
When she re-writes and reviews everything, she writes the same 65 letters again.
4. **Total letters written**:
Adding everything together:
\( 52 + 13 + 65 = 130 \).
