2. **Calculate the total weight of the 9 adults**:
   \[
   \text{Total weight} = \text{Number of adults} \times \text{Weight per adult}
   \]
   \[
   \text{Total weight} = 9 \times 80 = 720 \, \text{kg}
   \]

3. **Compare the total weight to the maximum load**:
   \[
   \text{Excess weight} = \text{Total weight} - \text{Maximum load}
   \]
   \[
   \text{Excess weight} = 720 - 700 = 20 \, \text{kg}
   \]

4. **Conclusion**: The total weight of the 9 adults exceeds the maximum load of the elevator by 20 kg.

